<title>USA: American Eagle disappointed with pilot vote.</title>
<headline>American Eagle disappointed with pilot vote.</headline>
<dateline>FORT WORTH, Texas 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Eagle said Monday it was disappointed that its pilots rejected a tentative labor agreement reached in May.</p>
<p>There were 642 pilots who opposed the tentative pact and 505 who voted for it, the pilots union said earlier Monday.</p>
<p>The pact would have covered all 1,900 pilots flying for the four regional carriers that operate under the Eagle name.</p>
<p>American Eagle pilots are currently on four separate senior lists on those carriers.</p>
<p>&quot;The airline will continue negotiations with its pilots union, the Air Line Pilots Association,&quot; an American Eagle statement said.</p>
</text>
